{"id": "EUVD-2026-96590", "enisaUuid": "a450cd5f-3789-32f5-b4c0-594b05626249", "description": "JeecgBoot through 3.9.5 contains a missing authorization vulnerability in the getRolesByUserId handler of SystemApiController that allows authenticated users to retrieve any user's role codes. Low-privileged attackers can supply arbitrary userId values to GET /sys/api/getRolesByUserId to enumerate role assignments and identify administrator accounts.", "datePublished": "2026-10-10T21:49:39", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T18:58:08", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/AnkesKasty/cve-request-poc/blob/a7b6d1423555812d8efa26c91c5d0683164b31e5/JeecgBoot/poc_c095_sys_api_roles.py", "https://github.com/jeecgboot/JeecgBoot/blob/e3b9dc0aefe1943d9772b026f64ed671a7c82802/jeecg-boot/jeecg-module-system/jeecg-system-biz/src/main/java/org/jeecg/modules/api/controller/SystemApiController.java#L155-L158", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/jeecgboot-through-3.9.5-missing-authorization-via-sys-api-getrolesbyuserid"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108651", "GHSA-p42c-xqf6-7f9q"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0ed65306-27a8-300d-a36e-cdae926171ed", "product": {"name": "JeecgBoot", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.9.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0447023c-6d8d-3487-87e1-8e03be70899e", "vendor": {"name": "jeecgboot"}}], "isExploited": false}